  {
    "path": "work\\fix_arms_hands_rightleg.py",
    "sha256": "2cdc0617a5bbb75e3c56006332ae2164b7683bc2904a77749ce3550e99211708",
    "bytes": 12928,
    "description": "Continue from the left-thigh repair.\n\n1. Islands that mix a hand bone with the body are resolved as either a rigid\n   weapon/shield or body skin. A consistent weapon island is not touched.\n2. Right thigh skin gets the same hip-to-leg falloff as the left thigh.\n3. Each shoulder cap blends spine, clavicle and upper arm along the bone."
  },
  {
    "path": "work\\fix_hip_thigh.py",
    "sha256": "299d63647774f177266753014acc95000dc163db6d2521ed69b1f3ae3af443a1",
    "bytes": 8617,
    "description": "Local hip/thigh skin blend for the verified body panel around 809011-809035.\n\nThe panel is thigh skin, not skirt cloth. Only this panel and its immediate\nsame-surface seam are reweighted. The blend file is written to a new path."
  },
  {
    "path": "work\\fix_hip_thigh_pass2.py",
    "sha256": "7f4e4baa1aa780c9bc3d51646da874f787039d10060bddd9a22c73f3e5ae75fa",
    "bytes": 8266,
    "description": "Redo the front-left thigh skin with a long hip-to-leg falloff.\n\nThe 2.5 cm band left a steep gradient: a 1.6 cm edge still posed to 9 cm.\nNative CK3 weights change across roughly the upper half of the thigh, so this\npass uses that length on this skin panel only. Source is the untouched work copy."
  },
  {
    "path": "work\\fix_hip_thigh_pass3.py",
    "sha256": "35631a576c00ee041004e25c82f199566b30d2ca473b67cd84c6d408436891d5",
    "bytes": 7501,
    "description": "Left-thigh skin only: hips to upper-leg falloff along the fitted thigh bone.\n\nPass 2 smoothed the original panel and then stopped mid-gradient, which moved\nthe tear to the mask border. This pass covers the left thigh skin whose weights\nare only Hips and LeftUpLeg, and it stops where the falloff is already pure.\nSkirt, hands, and the right leg are left unchanged. Source is the work copy."
  },
  {
    "path": "work\\fix_pass6.py",
